---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT } from "../consts";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What dynshift.com collects: nothing it can avoid. No cookies, no analytics, no advertising on this page.">
  <section class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="muted small">Last updated 15 September 2026.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>dynshift.com sets no cookies and runs no analytics.</strong> It
      is a set of static pages. There is nothing to sign up for, no form to
      fill in and no script that reports your visit anywhere.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. As with any web host, GitHub's
      servers see the request for each page, including your IP address, and
      handle it under
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
      DynShift does not receive or keep those logs.
    </p>
    <p>
      One tag in each page's head names an advertising account. It is a
      static site-ownership marker for Google AdSense: it loads nothing,
      stores nothing and shows nothing. <strong>No advertisements are served
      on dynshift.com.</strong>
    </p>

    <h2>Product sites</h2>
    <p>
      Each DynShift product lives on its own site with its own policy, which
      is the one that applies there:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://phonepad.dynshift.com/privacy/">PhonePad</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://layr.dynshift.com/" rel="noopener">Layr</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  section {
    padding-block: clamp(24px, 5vw, 56px);
  }
</style>
